.TH MINI-INIT-ASM 1 2026-09-05 "mini-init-asm 0.3.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mini-init-asm \- tiny PID 1 init for containers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mini-init-asm
[\fB-v\fR|\fB--verbose\fR]
[\fB-V\fR|\fB--version\fR]
\fB--\fR \fIcommand\fR [\fIargs\fR ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mini-init-asm
is a small container init that runs one child process as PID 1, forwards
incoming signals to the child's process group, and reaps exited descendants.
It is implemented in assembly and intentionally avoids libc runtime
dependencies.
.PP
On Debian, the installed executable is
.BR /usr/bin/mini-init-asm .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -v ", " --verbose
Enable verbose diagnostics on standard error.
.TP
.BR -V ", " --version
Print version information and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Numeric values are parsed as non-negative decimal integers. Invalid values are
ignored and defaults are used.
.TP
.B EP_SIGNALS
Comma-separated list of additional signals to monitor and forward to the child
process group. Tokens may be signal names (for example
.BR USR1 ,
.BR WINCH )
or signal numbers.
.TP
.B EP_SUBREAPER
If set to
.BR 1 ,
enable
.BR PR_SET_CHILD_SUBREAPER
so the process can adopt orphaned descendants before reaping them.
Default:
.BR 0 .
.TP
.B EP_RESTART_ENABLED
If set to
.BR 1 ,
restart the child when it dies from a signal and shutdown has not started.
Default:
.BR 0 .
.TP
.B EP_MAX_RESTARTS
Maximum number of restarts when
.B EP_RESTART_ENABLED=1
is active.
.BR 0
means unlimited restarts.
Default:
.BR 0 .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.IP \(bu 2
Returns the child's exit status when the child exits normally.
.IP \(bu 2
Returns a signal-based status when the child is terminated by a signal.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR signal (7),
.BR signalfd (2),
.BR prctl (2),
.BR wait4 (2)
